00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:56.149
Yeah, well so, of course other people are working on that sort of thing. And we do have theoretical evidence that supports the conjecture too.

00:11:56.939 --> 00:11:59.569
Some people think, though, that this problem is actually undecidable.

00:11:59.879 --> 00:12:03.678
So it might be that we never have a proof and this is as close as we can come,

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:04.610
okay?

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:07.369
So but - with each one of these stubborn candidates that we find

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:12.139
that gives another nail in the coffin of this idea that there aren't any more solutions.

00:12:12.269 --> 00:12:15.769
(Brady: So it's, so in a way knocking off these stubborn candidates - )

00:12:15.769 --> 00:12:19.248
(I've never heard that term before, I like it - knocking off these stubborn candidates)

00:12:19.559 --> 00:12:24.500
(is almost- you're giving hope to the people who are actually trying to come up with the rigorous proof?)

